  "notes": {
    "zone": "Zone 2 (the Ash Reach): the zone's own facts. `level` is the zone number = its base level (Dom 2026-10-08: Zone N = level N).",
    "spawns": "Zone 2's creatures as data (zone-runtime step 4, slice 1): the same six cited kinds as Zone 1 at the Zone 2 band (common [2, 3]: loadZone checks it), as PLACEHOLDERS until Characters\nship Zone 2's own creatures (a new kind needs a look in mob-looks.ts, a loot table and a character record; none is data-only yet). Every source is public-domain folklore, chronicle or literature (legends-rule).\n`openers`: Zone 2's one zone (the Region 2 layout, slice 3) opens with the wolf. Zone id -> row id. Donor: field names only (ModernUO spawn fields, Cataclysm place_monsters), nothing copied.",
    "kit": "Zone 2's kit (zone-runtime step 4, slice 1): Zone 1's kit (zone1-kit.glb) and density table until Characters ship a zone2 kit; the node names are that kit's contract. Read through loadZone only.",
    "look": "Zone 2's looks (slice 1): the same preset names the page asks for, with the Ash Reach's colder, duskier haze (Zone 1's values with the fog, sky and ground cooled). Read through loadZone only.",
    "mobLooks": "Zone 2's creature looks, as data: the Ember Wolf, the wolf body (public/world/wolf.glb, already in Zone 1's download: no new mesh) dressed ember red-brown instead of ash grey.\nscale = WOLF_RENDER_SCALE (2) x 1.1, a pack leader; a literal because zone data files hold one literal and `import type` only (the rule is src/fight/beast-scale.ts WOLF_RENDER_SCALE).",
    "place": "Zone 2 (the Ash Reach) on the Region 1 map: one open zone off the east road, its entry gate and a cairn at the middle. Its creatures are spawns.ts; this is where it stands and how the road reaches it."
